{"raw": {"https://employment.msubillings.edu/postings/7828": {"title": "Assistant/Associate Professor of Accounting", "description": "Montana State University Billings Employment Opportunities | Assistant/Associate Professor of Accounting Skip to Main Content Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Get the Details Employee Benefits About MSU Billings Location and Map Diversity/EEO Statement Explore Billings and the Region Human Resources Office Contact Us MSU BILLINGS HOME MSUB Annual Security & Fire Safety Report Notice of Availability Assistant/Associate Professor of Accounting Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Applicants must be currently authorized to work in the United States on a full-time basis without the need for employer sponsorship now or in the future. Applicants will be reviewed and interviewed on an ongoing basis after the screening date. The screening date begins 10 calendar days after a position is posted on the employment website. Position Details Position Information NBAPOSN Title Working Title Assistant/Associate Professor of Accounting Brief Position Overview Applicants are expected to teach undergraduate accounting courses required of the undergraduate major. Responsibilities include scholarly activity, academic advising, student mentoring, and college and university service appropriate for the appointed rank. Faculty Tenure Track Yes Faculty Rank Assistant Professor of Accounting Position Number Department College of Business Division College of Business Appointment Type Faculty Contract Term Academic Year Semester If other, specify From date If other, specify End date FLSA Union Affiliation Billings Faculty Association FTE 1.0 Benefits Eligible Yes Compensation Annual Salary Salary commensurate with experience, education, and qualifications. Contract Type MUS If other, please specify Recruitment Type Open Position Details General Statement Montana State University Billings is a preferred employer in the region-WE WANT YOU ! The following are reasons why you should join our team: Sick Leave \u2013 Earned per Contract Rate Employee and Dependent Tuition Waiver Opportunities to engage in professional development opportunities Committed to employee wellness and access to a robust Employee Assistance Program Medical Benefits that are robust and affordable Visit MUS Benefits to learn more about our benefit package including Medical, Vision, and Dental Life Insurance and Long-Term Disability are incorporated into our benefit Learn more about our retirement benefits at MUS Retirement Campus vibrancy- coffee shops, FREE attendance to MSUB concerts, athletic events, and lectures, access to recreation center, library, etc. Beautiful campus environment that features our MSUB Mile walking path Duties and Responsibilities Teaching: The successful candidate will teach a range of undergraduate accounting courses, including financial and managerial accounting. Preference will be given to candidates with expertise in auditing, and accounting information systems. Onsite, online and combination courses. Research: SA or SP status per AACSB (Association to Advance Collegiate Schools of Business) and maintain this status. Scholarly Academic (SA): Holds a terminal degree (such as a Ph.D.) and maintains ongoing currency through peer-reviewed research and academic publishing (per AACSB standards). SP (Scholarly Practitioner) master\u2019s degree or terminal degree in accounting or related degree. Substantial professional experience, and peer-reviewed publications/intellectual contributions (per AACSB standards). Please emphasis this, either with color, bold or some other method. Required Qualifications \u2013 Experience, Education, Knowledge & Skills Ph.D. in accounting or related field from an AACSB accredited business program. Strong candidates who are ABD and nearing completion of the dissertation may also be considered. Also considered are candidates with a master\u2019s in accounting and a CPA (only this license). Preferred Qualifications \u2013 Experience, Education, Knowledge & Skills Professional certification ( CPA ) Experience or interest in developing and updating curriculum. Interest and experience in providing learners with experiential learning opportunities. Willingness to engage with the broader community and cultivate partnerships that connect students to internships and professional opportunities across Montana State. Please address your current SA or SP status per AACSB (Association to Advance Collegiate Schools of Business) and your plans to maintain this status. Scholarly Academic (SA): Holds a terminal degree (such as a Ph.D.) and maintains ongoing currency through peer-reviewed research and academic publishing. Scholarly Practitioner (SP): Possesses a master\u2019s or terminal degree in a related field, and professional practice experience and scholarly research or writing in peer reviewed journals. Including your Research program that demonstrates an ability to contribute to College of Business\u2019 vision to be a model learning community of access and opportunity. Candidates teaching experience in multiple modalities within Accounting and Business. Experience with Big 4 audit or in education working with international universities. The Successful Candidate Will Have these qualities (evidence of the following in work history): Accountability/Dependability: Accepts responsibility for quality of own work; acknowledges and corrects mistakes. Shows up on time, meets standards, deadlines, and work schedules, including department meetings. Judgement: Makes timely, informed decisions. Analyzes options and determines appropriate course of action. Teamwork: Promotes cooperation and mutual support to achieve goals. Encourages participation and mutual support with students, faculty and administration. Adaptability/Flexibility: Responds positively to changing business needs and responsibilities. Adapts approach and methods to achieve results; recovers quickly from setbacks and finds alternatives. Commitment to Belonging: Values the uniqueness of every individual and fosters an environment where everyone feels respected and empowered to thrive. Special Requirements Physical Demands The Program The Department The College The College of Business at Montana State University Billings is a prominent regional business school holding prestigious AACSB accreditation\u2014a distinction earned by fewer than 6% of business schools worldwide. It offers a Bachelor of Science in Business Administration with five areas of emphasis, combining hands-on learning with strong employment outcomes. This position has supervisory duties? No Posting Detail Information Announcement Number FAC - VA - 2700003P Number of Vacancies 1 Desired Start Date 08/19/2027 Position End Date (if temporary) Open Date 10/01/2026 Close Date 12/15/2026 Open until filled Yes Special Instructions Summary Applicants must be currently authorized to work in the United States on a full-time basis without the need for employer sponsorship now or in the future. Applicants will be reviewed and interviewed on an ongoing basis after the screening date. The screening date begins 10 calendar days after a position is posted on the employment website. Quick Link for Internal Postings https://employment.msubillings.edu/postings/7810 Diversity Statement Montana State University Billings is committed to providing a working and learning environment free from discrimination. As such, the University does not discriminate in the admission, access to or conduct of its educational programs and activities nor in its employment policies and practices on the basis of race, color, religion, national origin, ethnicity, creed, service in the uniformed services (as defined in state and federal law), veteran status, gender, age, political beliefs, marital or family status, pregnancy, physical or mental disability, genetic information, gender identity, gender expression, or sexual orientation or preference. In support of the University\u2019s mission to be inclusive and diverse, applications from qualified minorities, women, veterans and persons with disabilities are highly encouraged. Montana State University Billings makes accommodation for any known disability that may interfere with an applicant\u2019s ability to compete in the hiring process or an employee\u2019s ability to perform the duties of the job. In compliance with the Montana Veteran\u2019s Employment Preference Act, MSU Billings provides preference in employment to veterans, disabled veterans, and certain eligible relatives of veterans. To claim veteran\u2019s preference or request accommodation, contact the Human Resources Office, Montana State University Billings, 1500 University Drive, Billings, MT 59101-0298, 406-657-2278, employment@msubillings.edu . MSU Billings Non-Discrimination Policy and Discrimination Grievance Procedures can be located on the MSU Billings Website: http://www.msubillings.edu/humres/eeos.htm Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume (or CV) Curriculum Vitae Cover Letter Transcript; unofficial is acceptable (5 MB max.) List of References (3 or more) Optional Documents Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). 1500 University Drive | Billings, MT 59101 | 406.657.2278 | \u00a9 2014 Montana State University Billings | employment@msubillings.edu To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://employment.msubillings.edu/postings/7821": {"title": "Assistant Professor of English, Writing, and Composition", "description": "Montana State University Billings Employment Opportunities | Assistant Professor of English, Writing, and Composition Skip to Main Content Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Get the Details Employee Benefits About MSU Billings Location and Map Diversity/EEO Statement Explore Billings and the Region Human Resources Office Contact Us MSU BILLINGS HOME MSUB Annual Security & Fire Safety Report Notice of Availability Assistant Professor of English, Writing, and Composition Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Applicants will be reviewed and interviewed on an ongoing basis after the screening date. The screening date begins 10 calendar days after a position is posted on the employment website. Applicants must be currently authorized to work in the United States on a full-time basis without the need for employer sponsorship now or in the future. Position Details Position Information NBAPOSN Title Working Title Assistant Professor of English, Writing, and Composition Brief Position Overview The Department of English, Philosophy and Modern Languages invites applications for an Assistant Professor of English, Writing, and Composition or a closely related field to begin fall 2027. The successful candidate will be primarily responsible for teaching undergraduate courses in English composition with the possibility of teaching other writing and literature courses during the academic year. Opportunities to develop additional courses in the candidate\u2019s specialty area exist. The successful candidate will also hold the position of Writing Program Coordinator, which includes conducting peer reviews of part-time composition instructors, providing pedagogical support for composition faculty, meeting with writing instructors, developing methods for composition placement, assessing the effectiveness of the composition program (including the placement of students and the usefulness of the enhanced composition courses), and overseeing and developing a comprehensive plan across the university for the composition program. Other expected duties include advising students; service to the department, college, and/or university committees; contributions to the department\u2019s ongoing assessment and curricular needs; and an active research, presentation, and publication agenda. A secondary expertise in Creative Writing is preferred. The teaching load for Assistant Professor at MSUB is 21 credits for the academic year with reassigned time for the position of Writing Program Coordinator. Summer teaching opportunities are available but are not required. Faculty Tenure Track Yes Faculty Rank Assistant Professor Position Number Department Eng Phil & Mod Languages Division College of Liberal Arts & Social Sciences Appointment Type Faculty Contract Term Academic Year Semester If other, specify From date If other, specify End date FLSA Union Affiliation Billings Faculty Association FTE 1.0 Benefits Eligible Yes Compensation Annual Salary Salary commensurate with experience, education, and qualifications. Contract Type MUS If other, please specify Recruitment Type Open Position Details General Statement Montana State University Billings is a preferred employer in the region-WE WANT YOU ! The following are reasons why you should join our team: Sick Leave \u2013 Earned per Contract Rate Employee and Dependent Tuition Waiver Opportunities to engage in professional development opportunities Committed to employee wellness and access to a robust Employee Assistance Program Medical Benefits that are robust and affordable Visit MUS Benefits to learn more about our benefit package including Medical, Vision, and Dental Life Insurance and Long-Term Disability are incorporated into our benefits Learn more about our retirement benefits at MUS Retirement Campus vibrancy- coffee shops, FREE attendance to MSUB concerts, athletic events, and lectures, access to recreation center, library, etc. Beautiful campus environment that features our MSUB Mile walking path Duties and Responsibilities The Department of English, Philosophy and Modern Languages invites applications for an Assistant Professor of English, Writing, and Composition or a closely related field to begin fall 2027. The successful candidate will be primarily responsible for teaching undergraduate courses in English composition with the possibility of teaching other writing and literature courses during the academic year. Opportunities to develop additional courses in the candidate\u2019s specialty area exist. The successful candidate will also hold the position of Writing Program Coordinator, which includes conducting peer reviews of part-time composition instructors, providing pedagogical support for composition faculty, meeting with writing instructors, developing methods for composition placement, assessing the effectiveness of the composition program (including the placement of students and the usefulness of the enhanced composition courses), and overseeing and developing a comprehensive plan across the university for the composition program. Other expected duties include advising students; service to the department, college, and/or university committees; contributions to the department\u2019s ongoing assessment and curricular needs; and an active research, presentation, and publication agenda. A secondary expertise in Creative Writing is preferred. The teaching load for Assistant Professor at MSUB is 21 credits for the academic year with reassigned time for the position of Writing Program Coordinator. Summer teaching opportunities are available but are not required. Required Qualifications \u2013 Experience, Education, Knowledge & Skills PhD in English, Composition, or closely related field ( ABD considered) Appropriate background in the needed area(s) of specialization Ability and interest in undergraduate teaching Experience teaching professional and/or technical writing Experience with and commitment to working with diverse student populations Ability and willingness to develop and teach sections/courses using onsite, online, hybrid, and/or Hyflex delivery methods Preferred Qualifications \u2013 Experience, Education, Knowledge & Skills Experience with teaching second-year composition and grant writing Experience working with first generation students Experience teaching creative writing The Successful Candidate Will Special Requirements Physical Demands The Program The Department The College This position has supervisory duties? No Posting Detail Information Announcement Number FAC - VA - 2700004P Number of Vacancies Desired Start Date Position End Date (if temporary) Open Date 10/02/2026 Close Date 01/01/2027 Open until filled Yes Special Instructions Summary Applicants will be reviewed and interviewed on an ongoing basis after the screening date. The screening date begins 10 calendar days after a position is posted on the employment website. Applicants must be currently authorized to work in the United States on a full-time basis without the need for employer sponsorship now or in the future. Quick Link for Internal Postings https://employment.msubillings.edu/postings/7817 Diversity Statement Montana State University Billings is committed to providing a working and learning environment free from discrimination. As such, the University does not discriminate in the admission, access to or conduct of its educational programs and activities nor in its employment policies and practices on the basis of race, color, religion, national origin, ethnicity, creed, service in the uniformed services (as defined in state and federal law), veteran status, gender, age, political beliefs, marital or family status, pregnancy, physical or mental disability, genetic information, gender identity, gender expression, or sexual orientation or preference. In support of the University\u2019s mission to be inclusive and diverse, applications from qualified minorities, women, veterans and persons with disabilities are highly encouraged. Montana State University Billings makes accommodation for any known disability that may interfere with an applicant\u2019s ability to compete in the hiring process or an employee\u2019s ability to perform the duties of the job. In compliance with the Montana Veteran\u2019s Employment Preference Act, MSU Billings provides preference in employment to veterans, disabled veterans, and certain eligible relatives of veterans. To claim veteran\u2019s preference or request accommodation, contact the Human Resources Office, Montana State University Billings, 1500 University Drive, Billings, MT 59101-0298, 406-657-2278, employment@msubillings.edu . MSU Billings Non-Discrimination Policy and Discrimination Grievance Procedures can be located on the MSU Billings Website: http://www.msubillings.edu/humres/eeos.htm Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vitae Cover Letter List of References (3 or more) Philosophy Statement Teaching Evaluations Research Agenda Optional Documents Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). 1500 University Drive | Billings, MT 59101 | 406.657.2278 | \u00a9 2014 Montana State University Billings | employment@msubillings.edu To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://employment.msubillings.edu/postings/7804": {"title": "Assistant/Associate Professor of Criminal Justice", "description": "Montana State University Billings Employment Opportunities | Assistant/Associate Professor of Criminal Justice Skip to Main Content Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Get the Details Employee Benefits About MSU Billings Location and Map Diversity/EEO Statement Explore Billings and the Region Human Resources Office Contact Us MSU BILLINGS HOME MSUB Annual Security & Fire Safety Report Notice of Availability Assistant/Associate Professor of Criminal Justice Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Applications received by October 12, 2026 will be given preference, though the position will remain open until filled. Applicants will be reviewed and interviewed on an ongoing basis after the screening date. The screening date begins 10 calendar days after a position is posted on the employment website. Applicants must be currently authorized to work in the United States on a full-time basis without the need for employer sponsorship now or in the future. Position Details Position Information NBAPOSN Title Working Title Assistant/Associate Professor of Criminal Justice Brief Position Overview ABOUT THE COLLEGE : The mission of the College of Liberal Arts & Social Sciences is to serve the educational needs of the people of Montana through academic programs leading to Baccalaureate Degrees in the liberal arts and social sciences; selected graduate programs leading to a Master\u2019s Degree; General Education courses providing a foundation of liberal education to all students at MSU Billings; selected pre-professional programs and various graduate, continuing education and non-conventional learning opportunities consistent with the mission of the University. Through these learning experiences, the College seeks to provide knowledge and cultivate skills to allow a student to select realistic future directions for study and/or employment. With its inherent diversity, the College is an intellectual and cultural resource for all students, faculty, and staff of the University and for the community and region. Faculty Tenure Track Yes Faculty Rank Assistant/Associate Professor Position Number 6A0203 Department Dept of Soc Sciences & Cultural Stu Division College of Liberal Arts & Social Sciences Appointment Type Faculty Contract Term Academic Year Semester If other, specify From date If other, specify End date FLSA Union Affiliation Billings Faculty Association FTE 1.0 Benefits Eligible Compensation Bi-Weekly Salary Commensurate with education and experience and subject to the Collective Bargaining Agreement (CBA) Montana State University-Billings Faculty Association Contract Type MUS If other, please specify Recruitment Type Open Position Details General Statement Montana State University Billings is the third largest University in Montana and is located in Montana\u2019s largest city. The University has five colleges, through which it serves a diverse student body and a broad regional community. Our staff and faculty strive to transform the lives of our students by empowering them to succeed in achieving their educational and life goals. To give our students the best possible path to success in achieving their goals, we are committed to closing equity gaps via our recruitment, retention, and completion initiatives. MSUB faculty and students are also active in scholarship and creative endeavors on state-wide, national, and international stages. Our programs are responsive to community needs and partner with local and regional entities to provide clinical, internship and experiential learning opportunities to our students. MSUB is an innovator in teaching strategies and modalities that accommodate students\u2019 individual learning needs and busy lifestyles. Interested individuals can obtain more information about Montana State University Billings at https://www.msubillings.edu . Duties and Responsibilities The Department of Social Sciences and Cultural Studies invites applications for an Assistant or Associate Professor of Criminal Justice to begin fall 2027. This is a tenure-track position, and the successful candidate will teach undergraduate courses including careers in criminal justice, applied research methods, crime theory and data, and criminal justice ethics, and graduate courses including graduate research methods, data analysis and management, advanced crime theory and data, ethics and public policy, and special topics. Opportunities to develop additional courses in the candidate\u2019s specialty area exist. Criminal Justice is the second largest program in the college and is situated within an interdisciplinary department. Degree offerings include the AS and BS criminal justice, and a new MS in criminal justice that began with the fall 2025 semester. MSUB serves students from across the state and region, and our department is committed to offering courses that allow both our in-person and our online students to achieve timely graduation. The teaching load for tenure track faculty at MSUB is 21 credits per year. To meet departmental needs, the individual chosen for this position will teach 3 courses each fall semester and 4 courses each spring semester. Summer teaching opportunities are available but are not required. The successful candidate will also serve as graduate coordinator for the department\u2019s MS in Criminal Justice. In addition to these teaching obligations, faculty at MSUB are expected to engage in scholarship and service activities. These expectations are outlined in the collective bargaining agreement (available on the university website) and in department rank and tenure guidelines (available from the department chair). To apply, please submit: (1) A cover letter highlighting your interest teaching at MSUB , your ability to teach courses on research methods and criminal justice ethics , and your experience with in-person, online, and/or multi-modality teaching; (2) A curriculum vitae; (3) Unofficial transcripts of all graduate work (official transcripts will be requested at the time of hire); (4) Teaching evaluations or other evidence of teaching excellence; (5) A representative sample of scholarly work; and (6) Statements of teaching philosophy and research agenda. Letters of recommendation are not required during the initial application process, though shortlisted candidates should expect to provide contact information for three professional references. Required Qualifications \u2013 Experience, Education, Knowledge & Skills PhD in criminal justice, criminology, or related field ( ABD considered) Willingness to teach at both the undergraduate and graduate levels Expertise in quantitative research methods. Preferred Qualifications \u2013 Experience, Education, Knowledge & Skills Ability to teach a restricted elective course on victimology and/or inequality Experience teaching in-person, online, or using multiple-format modalities Experience working with first generation students The Successful Candidate Will Special Requirements Physical Demands The Program The Department The College This position has supervisory duties? No Posting Detail Information Announcement Number FAC - VA - 2700002P Number of Vacancies Desired Start Date Position End Date (if temporary) Open Date 09/02/2026 Close Date 10/12/2026 Open until filled Yes Special Instructions Summary Applications received by October 12, 2026 will be given preference, though the position will remain open until filled. Applicants will be reviewed and interviewed on an ongoing basis after the screening date. The screening date begins 10 calendar days after a position is posted on the employment website. Applicants must be currently authorized to work in the United States on a full-time basis without the need for employer sponsorship now or in the future. Quick Link for Internal Postings https://employment.msubillings.edu/postings/7796 Diversity Statement Montana State University Billings is committed to providing a working and learning environment free from discrimination. As such, the University does not discriminate in the admission, access to or conduct of its educational programs and activities nor in its employment policies and practices on the basis of race, color, religion, national origin, ethnicity, creed, service in the uniformed services (as defined in state and federal law), veteran status, gender, age, political beliefs, marital or family status, pregnancy, physical or mental disability, genetic information, gender identity, gender expression, or sexual orientation or preference. In support of the University\u2019s mission to be inclusive and diverse, applications from qualified minorities, women, veterans and persons with disabilities are highly encouraged. Montana State University Billings makes accommodation for any known disability that may interfere with an applicant\u2019s ability to compete in the hiring process or an employee\u2019s ability to perform the duties of the job. In compliance with the Montana Veteran\u2019s Employment Preference Act, MSU Billings provides preference in employment to veterans, disabled veterans, and certain eligible relatives of veterans. To claim veteran\u2019s preference or request accommodation, contact the Human Resources Office, Montana State University Billings, 1500 University Drive, Billings, MT 59101-0298, 406-657-2278, employment@msubillings.edu . MSU Billings Non-Discrimination Policy and Discrimination Grievance Procedures can be located on the MSU Billings Website: http://www.msubillings.edu/humres/eeos.htm Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vitae Cover Letter Transcript; unofficial is acceptable (5 MB max.) List of References (3 or more) Teaching Evaluations Research Agenda PDF Examples of Work Optional Documents Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). 1500 University Drive | Billings, MT 59101 | 406.657.2278 | \u00a9 2014 Montana State University Billings | employment@msubillings.edu To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://employment.msubillings.edu/postings/7798": {"title": "Assistant or Associate Professor of Criminal Justice", "description": "Montana State University Billings Employment Opportunities | Assistant or Associate Professor of Criminal Justice Skip to Main Content Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Get the Details Employee Benefits About MSU Billings Location and Map Diversity/EEO Statement Explore Billings and the Region Human Resources Office Contact Us MSU BILLINGS HOME MSUB Annual Security & Fire Safety Report Notice of Availability Assistant or Associate Professor of Criminal Justice Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. REVIEW DATE: Applications received by October 12, 2026 will be given preference, though the position will remain open until filled. Applicants will be reviewed and interviewed on an ongoing basis after the screening date. The screening date begins 10 calendar days after a position is posted on the employment website. Applicants must be currently authorized to work in the United States on a full-time basis without the need for employer sponsorship now or in the future. Position Details Position Information NBAPOSN Title Working Title Assistant or Associate Professor of Criminal Justice Brief Position Overview ABOUT THE COLLEGE : The mission of the College of Liberal Arts & Social Sciences is to serve the educational needs of the people of Montana through academic programs leading to Baccalaureate Degrees in the liberal arts and social sciences; selected graduate programs leading to a Master\u2019s Degree; General Education courses providing a foundation of liberal education to all students at MSU Billings; selected pre-professional programs and various graduate, continuing education and non-conventional learning opportunities consistent with the mission of the University. Through these learning experiences, the College seeks to provide knowledge and cultivate skills to allow a student to select realistic future directions for study and/or employment. With its inherent diversity, the College is an intellectual and cultural resource for all students, faculty, and staff of the University and for the community and region. Faculty Tenure Track Yes Faculty Rank Assistant/Associate Position Number 6A0944 Department Dept of Soc Sciences & Cultural Stu Division Appointment Type Faculty Contract Term Academic Year Semester If other, specify From date If other, specify End date FLSA Union Affiliation Billings Faculty Association FTE 1.0 Benefits Eligible Yes Compensation Bi-Weekly Salary Salary commensurate with education and experience and subject to the Collective Bargaining Agreement (CBA) Montana State University-Billings Faculty Association Contract Type MUS If other, please specify Recruitment Type Open Position Details General Statement Montana State University Billings is the third largest University in Montana and is located in Montana\u2019s largest city. The University has five colleges, through which it serves a diverse student body and a broad regional community. Our staff and faculty strive to transform the lives of our students by empowering them to succeed in achieving their educational and life goals. To give our students the best possible path to success in achieving their goals, we are committed to closing equity gaps via our recruitment, retention, and completion initiatives. MSUB faculty and students are also active in scholarship and creative endeavors on state-wide, national, and international stages. Our programs are responsive to community needs and partner with local and regional entities to provide clinical, internship and experiential learning opportunities to our students. MSUB is an innovator in teaching strategies and modalities that accommodate students\u2019 individual learning needs and busy lifestyles. Interested individuals can obtain more information about Montana State University Billings at https://www.msubillings.edu . Duties and Responsibilities The Department of Social Sciences and Cultural Studies invites applications for an Assistant or Associate Professor of Criminal Justice to begin fall 2027. This is a tenure-track position, and the successful candidate will teach undergraduate courses including introductory and advanced courses on policing, introductory and advanced courses on the courts, and graduate courses including criminal justice policy, multicultural issues in criminal justice, and special topics. Opportunities to develop additional courses in the candidate\u2019s specialty area exist. Criminal Justice is the second largest program in the college and is situated within an interdisciplinary department. Degree offerings include the AS and BS criminal justice, and a new MS in criminal justice that began with the fall 2025 semester. MSUB serves students from across the state and region, and our department is committed to offering courses that allow both our in-person and our online students to achieve timely graduation. The teaching load for tenure track faculty at MSUB is 21 credits per year. To meet departmental needs, the individual chosen for this position will teach 3 courses each fall semester and 4 courses each spring semester. Summer teaching opportunities are available but are not required. In addition to these teaching obligations, faculty at MSUB are expected to engage in scholarship and service activities. These expectations are outlined in the collective bargaining agreement (available on the university website) and in department rank and tenure guidelines (available from the department chair). To apply, please submit: (1) A cover letter highlighting your interest teaching at MSUB , your ability to teach courses on policing and the courts, and your experience with in-person, online, and/or multi-modality teaching; (2) A curriculum vitae; (3) Unofficial transcripts of all graduate work (official transcripts will be requested at the time of hire); (4) Teaching evaluations or other evidence of teaching excellence; (5) A representative sample of scholarly work; and (6) Statements of teaching philosophy and research agenda. Letters of recommendation are not required during the initial application process, though shortlisted candidates should expect to provide contact information for three professional references. Required Qualifications \u2013 Experience, Education, Knowledge & Skills PhD in criminal justice, criminology, or related field ( ABD considered) Expertise in policing and the courts Preferred Qualifications \u2013 Experience, Education, Knowledge & Skills Ability to teach a restricted elective course on victimology and/or inequality Experience teaching in-person, online, or using multiple-format modalities Willingness to teach at both the undergraduate and graduate levels Experience working with first generation students The Successful Candidate Will Special Requirements Physical Demands The Program The Department The College This position has supervisory duties? No Posting Detail Information Announcement Number FAC - VA - 2700001P Number of Vacancies Desired Start Date 08/11/2027 Position End Date (if temporary) Open Date 08/31/2026 Close Date 10/12/2026 Open until filled Yes Special Instructions Summary REVIEW DATE : Applications received by October 12, 2026 will be given preference, though the position will remain open until filled. Applicants will be reviewed and interviewed on an ongoing basis after the screening date. The screening date begins 10 calendar days after a position is posted on the employment website. Applicants must be currently authorized to work in the United States on a full-time basis without the need for employer sponsorship now or in the future. Quick Link for Internal Postings https://employment.msubillings.edu/postings/7794 Diversity Statement Montana State University Billings is committed to providing a working and learning environment free from discrimination. As such, the University does not discriminate in the admission, access to or conduct of its educational programs and activities nor in its employment policies and practices on the basis of race, color, religion, national origin, ethnicity, creed, service in the uniformed services (as defined in state and federal law), veteran status, gender, age, political beliefs, marital or family status, pregnancy, physical or mental disability, genetic information, gender identity, gender expression, or sexual orientation or preference. In support of the University\u2019s mission to be inclusive and diverse, applications from qualified minorities, women, veterans and persons with disabilities are highly encouraged. Montana State University Billings makes accommodation for any known disability that may interfere with an applicant\u2019s ability to compete in the hiring process or an employee\u2019s ability to perform the duties of the job. In compliance with the Montana Veteran\u2019s Employment Preference Act, MSU Billings provides preference in employment to veterans, disabled veterans, and certain eligible relatives of veterans. To claim veteran\u2019s preference or request accommodation, contact the Human Resources Office, Montana State University Billings, 1500 University Drive, Billings, MT 59101-0298, 406-657-2278, employment@msubillings.edu . MSU Billings Non-Discrimination Policy and Discrimination Grievance Procedures can be located on the MSU Billings Website: http://www.msubillings.edu/humres/eeos.htm Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vitae Cover Letter Transcript; unofficial is acceptable (5 MB max.) List of References (3 or more) Teaching Evaluations Research Agenda Optional Documents Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). 1500 University Drive | Billings, MT 59101 | 406.657.2278 | \u00a9 2014 Montana State University Billings | employment@msubillings.edu To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://employment.msubillings.edu/postings/7601": {"title": "Part Time Faculty", "description": "Montana State University Billings Employment Opportunities | Part Time Faculty Skip to Main Content Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Get the Details Employee Benefits About MSU Billings Location and Map Diversity/EEO Statement Explore Billings and the Region Human Resources Office Contact Us MSU BILLINGS HOME MSUB Annual Security & Fire Safety Report Notice of Availability Part Time Faculty Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Position Information NBAPOSN Title Working Title Part Time Faculty Brief Position Overview ABOUT MONTANA STATE UNIVERSITY BILLINGS Montana State University Billings is the third largest University in Montana and is located in Montana\u2019s largest city. The University has five colleges, through which it serves a diverse student body and a broad regional community. Our staff and faculty strive to transform the lives of our students by empowering them to succeed in achieving their educational and life goals. To give our students the best possible path to success in achieving their goals, we are committed to closing equity gaps via our recruitment, retention, and completion initiatives. MSUB faculty and students are also active in scholarship and creative endeavors on state-wide, national, and international stages. Our programs are responsive to community needs and partner with local and regional entities to provide clinical, internship and experiential learning opportunities to our students. MSUB is an innovator in teaching strategies and modalities that accommodate students\u2019 individual learning needs and busy lifestyles. Interested individuals can obtain more information about Montana State University Billings at https://www.msubillings.edu Faculty Tenure Track No Faculty Rank Part Time Position Number Department Provost & VC Academic Affairs Division Academic Affairs Appointment Type Faculty Contract Term Other Semester If other, specify From date If other, specify End date FLSA Union Affiliation FTE Benefits Eligible No Compensation Annual Salary Salary is based on credit hour and modality of teaching. Contract Type MUS If other, please specify Recruitment Type Open Position Details General Statement ABOUT THE COLLEGE : Montana State University Billings is a comprehensive public four year higher education institution located in Montana\u2019s largest population center, whose faculty is actively engaged in teaching, research, creative endeavors and public service. MSU Billings is unique in that it is one of a select few higher education institutions that also boasts an embedded two-year community college. The University opened in 1927 and was initially called Eastern Montana State Normal School at Billings and was established to prepare teachers for elementary schools in eastern Montana. MSU Billings has grown, with the city of Billings and Yellowstone County, into the major urban comprehensive higher education center of south central and eastern Montana. The University Campus consists of four colleges: the College of Arts and Sciences, the College of Business, the College of Education and the College of Allied Health Professions. Seven miles west of the University campus sits City College at MSU Billings, which serves the comprehensive t wo-year mission of the university. Duties and Responsibilities Montana State University Billings is a preferred employer in the region-WE WANT YOU ! The following are reasons why you should join our team: Work-life balance Opportunities to engage in professional development opportunities Campus vibrancy- coffee shops, FREE attendance to MSUB concerts, athletic events, and lectures, access to recreation center, library, etc. Beautiful campus environment that features our MSUB Mile walking path Required Qualifications \u2013 Experience, Education, Knowledge & Skills Preferred Qualifications \u2013 Experience, Education, Knowledge & Skills The Successful Candidate Will Special Requirements Physical Demands The Program The Department The College This position has supervisory duties? No Posting Detail Information Announcement Number F00293P 